# ── Credentials & Secrets ─────────────────────────────────────────
confidentials/*
!confidentials/.env.template
.env
*.env
outlook_token.json

# Written into an applied update's package by release.py, read by
# mcp_server._get_code_version() so version tracking survives .git being
# excluded from every update package. Never hand-author or commit this --
# it's a build-time artifact, stale the moment it's checked in.
/VERSION

# ── Data ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
data/logs/*

# CoStar exports and broker spreadsheets dropped here for screening.
# Business data -- never commit it.
data/drop/*

# Defensive net for any ad hoc "*backup*" folder anyone creates directly
# under data/. Kept from the ChromaDB era, where a ~55MB database backup
# under a variant name once slipped through and got committed to git
# history. The vector DB is gone, but the pattern still costs nothing and
# the failure it prevents is expensive to undo.
data/*backup*/

# ── Processed Files (ingested documents) ──────────────────────────
data/processed/*

# ── Watched Folder (drop zone — not committed) ────────────────────
data/watched_folder/*

# ── Project Master (real file stays local) ────────────────────────
data/project_master/*
!data/project_master/.gitkeep

# Local stand-in for the shared team OneDrive folder (proximity_output,
# screening_output, property_summaries, updates, org_settings), used only
# when config.py can't find OneDrive on this machine. Same real firm data
# as the OneDrive version -- data/ is otherwise fully gitignored, but this
# one didn't have its own explicit line, so it wasn't actually covered.
data/shared_fallback_not_synced/*

# ── Confidential business documents (repo is deliberately PUBLIC) ──
# This repo is public on purpose -- it's a portfolio piece. These docs
# hold the firm's real deal names, prices, addresses, and counterparty
# names, derived from its private document library. They stay local:
# untracked 2026-07-29 after being confirmed publicly fetchable.
# The evidence appendix collects the real figures that used to be
# cited inline in CLAUDE.md / REBUILD_PLAN.md / fit_screen.py.
docs/PORTFOLIO_STANDARD.md
docs/COMPANY_PROFILE.md
docs/jurisdictions/
docs/EVIDENCE_APPENDIX.md

# Per-agent audit logs: they record real property names, real export
# filenames, and real findings from each run. The context.md files
# (tracked) describe the agents; the logs stay local.
docs/agents/*/memory.md

# ── Corpus index (generated, machine-specific, and sensitive) ──────
# corpus/index.py builds this SQLite index of the firm's SharePoint
# library. It holds no file CONTENTS -- but it does hold ~493,000
# file and folder NAMES, and those names alone disclose plenty:
# entity names, deal names, counterparties, and live litigation
# ("Hoffman v. Forshpan Documents"). It is also rebuildable in ~2
# minutes via `python main.py index-corpus`, so there is nothing to
# gain by committing it and a real disclosure risk if we do.
data/corpus_index.db
data/corpus_index.db-journal
data/corpus_index.db-wal

# ── Auto-update staging (local, transient -- code zips + org-wide ──
# setting values in plain text; the latter can be real API keys, so
# this must never be committed, not even by accident via `git add -A`)
data/pending_update/*
data/pending_settings/*

# ── Keep folder structure via .gitkeep ────────────────────────────
!data/logs/.gitkeep
!data/processed/.gitkeep
!data/watched_folder/.gitkeep

# ── Python ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.pyo
*.pyd
.Python
*.egg-info/
dist/
build/
.eggs/

# ── Virtual Environment ───────────────────────────────────────────
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/

# ── Logs ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.log

# ── PyCharm ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.idea/
*.iml

# ── VS Code ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.vscode/

# ── Claude Code (personal per-machine config stays local) ─────────
.claude/settings.local.json

# The confidential-name blocklist read by .claude/hooks/check_no_leaks.py.
# The hook script itself is tracked (the mechanism is good portfolio
# material); this list is the actual secret and must never be. See that
# script's docstring.
.claude/hooks/leak_patterns.txt

# ── Windows ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/

# ── Mac ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride